  "notes": "Elm Company (ticker 7203, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/2784_0_2026-03-05...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co.; unqualified opinion. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on Ramadan 9, 1447H (corresponding to 26 February 2026) - Note 43. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1). The primary statements (printed FS pages 6-10) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the notes (printed pages 11-59) are digital text. Consolidated group with a very small non-controlling interest (NCI equity SAR 112,771; NCI share of loss SAR -28,111 in FY2025). There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies (income_before_income_taxes_and_zakat is the reported 'NET PROFIT BEFORE ZAKAT'). Note 40: on 21 April 2025 Elm completed the acquisition of 100% of Thiqah Business Services Company from the Public Investment Fund for an adjusted consideration of SAR 3,385.9 million; because both entities are under PIF common control it was accounted for as a business combination under common control, with the SAR 3,121,807,695 excess of consideration over net assets acquired taken directly to retained earnings (statement of changes in equity) rather than to goodwill - this is the main driver of the FY2025 fall in retained earnings and of the SAR -3,141,074,348 'Payment for acquisition of subsidiary' investing outflow and the SAR 1,900,000,000 new long-term borrowing. impairment_charges combines the two P&L expense lines 'Expected credit losses' (SAR -105,710,338; FY2024 -142,748,596) and 'Impairment of non-current assets' (SAR -30,210,394; FY2024 -21,343,476). depreciation_amortization is the P&L opex line 'Depreciation and amortization' (also shown as the cash-flow add-back at the same amount). selling_and_distribution_expense is the reported 'Selling and marketing' expense. finance_costs is 'Finance cost'; finance_income is 'Income from murabaha deposits'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Share in results from investments in associates and joint ventures' (a loss both years); other_nonoperating_income is 'Change in fair value of financial assets through profit or loss, net'; other_income is the reported 'Other income, net' (Note 10 - mainly HRDF Saudization support and call-account income). income_taxes_and_zakat is 'Zakat, net'. On the balance sheet: construction_in_progress is 'Capital work in progress'; long_term_investments is the non-current 'Other financial assets'; investments_associates is 'Investments in associates and joint ventures'; other_noncurrent_assets combines 'Finance lease receivables - non current' and 'Long term prepaid expenses'; contract_assets and contract_liabilities are the reported lines; short_term_investments is 'Murabaha deposits' (term > 3 months, Note 21); other_current_assets combines the current 'Other financial assets' and 'Finance lease receivables - current'; prepayments is 'Prepaid expenses and other current assets'; treasury_shares is the negative 'Treasury shares' line; other_reserves is the reported 'Other reserves' (Note 27 - EOSB remeasurement, FVOCI reserve, share-based-payment reserve and FX translation); defined_benefit_obligation is 'End of service benefits provision'; zakat_payable is the 'Zakat' current-liability line; long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current and current portions of 'Long term borrowing' (both nil in FY2024, so no FY2024 fact is carried for them); lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current are the reported lease-liability portions. On the cash-flow statement: operating_cash_flow / investing_cash_flow / financing_cash_flow are the three net subtotals; capex combines 'Purchase of property, equipment and intangible assets' and 'Payments for capital work in progress'; acquisitions is 'Payment for acquisition of subsidiary, net of cash acquired' (FY2025 only); debt_issued is 'Addition to long term borrowing' (FY2025 only); lease_payments is 'Payment of principal portion of lease liabilities'; interest_paid is 'Finance costs paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid'; foreign_exchange_effect is 'Net foreign currency exchange'; the cash-flow closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. FY2024 comparatives include a minor P&L reclassification of SAR 5,371,520 between cost of revenue and general and administrative expenses (Note 39); the figures carried here are the reported post-reclassification amounts as presented on the FY2025 face statements. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: profit or loss 6, comprehensive income 7, financial position 8, changes in equity 9, cash flows 10.",
